On agent-framework, Wiz (disclosure: the site's author works at Wiz): "We have not linked the two incidents."
notes:
The page links three other kill chains on csoh.org.

Mini Shai-Hulud is the worm Miasma rebrands. TeamPCP published its source, and the site's page treats TeamPCP's role in that worm as claimed, not proven. That page and CHAINDROP's document the same Claude Code SessionStart hook and VS Code folder-open task, and both give the same response order for their own watchers as the CSA does here.

Microsoft's agent-framework package was hijacked on PyPI in November by a different route. That page quotes Wiz saying it has not linked the two incidents. As the page discloses, the site's author works at Wiz.

The defense topics cover GitHub Actions, CI/CD security, AI and ML security, non-human identity and incident response.
